# Documentation Governance

- **Authority:** existing docs unless contradicted by current code or tests.
- **New design specs:** `docs/superpowers/specs/NNN-YYYY-MM-DD-<kind>-<layer>-<area>-<topic>-design.md`
- **New implementation plans:** `docs/superpowers/plans/NNN-YYYY-MM-DD-<kind>-<layer>-<area>-prNN-<topic>.md`
- **Naming detail:** [AGENTS.md § Spec & plan file naming](mdc:AGENTS.md) — directory-local `NNN`; `prNN` plan-only; `risk` in frontmatter; legacy docs grandfathered; active canonical docs may rename per AGENTS rename criteria
- **Program roadmaps:** `docs/superpowers/roadmap/NNN-YYYY-MM-DD-<area>-<topic>-roadmap.md` (orientation only; spec still required per wave)
- **Index:** [docs/superpowers/README.md](mdc:docs/superpowers/README.md)
- **Architecture / runtime truth:** [docs/current_architecture.md](mdc:docs/current_architecture.md), [pyproject.toml](mdc:pyproject.toml)
- **Historical research and old plans:** [documents/](mdc:documents/README.md) — do not add new specs/plans here
- **Archive:** [docs/archive/](mdc:docs/archive/README.md) — may be stale; prefer current_architecture for behavior
- Do not silently change public contracts without a spec and drift note in the plan.
